  "published": "2026-08-25T16:01:28.04Z",
  "releaseNotes": "TCMProject.Utilities: adds the Platform_* permission catalogue (values 33-43) plus a ServiceEnum.PLATFORM and three modules (PLATFORM_TENANTS, PLATFORM_BILLING, PLATFORM_PAYMENTS). These gate the TCM Admin panel — viewing tenants and billing, creating and approving discounts, running the billing cycle by hand, and the payments module: viewing collections, reconciling by hand, refunding, configuring which methods a Merchant accepts, and managing gateway credentials. They live in the SAME enum as the clinical permissions on purpose (decision P1/P2 of platform-permissions-design.md): the Role -> RolePermission -> PermissionEnum engine already existed and duplicating it would have meant two permission systems ageing apart; what separates them is the module, not the storage. Appended at the end per the enum architecture rule, so no existing value moves. Backward-safe: the stored byte array grows from 5 to 6 bytes, and HasPermission already guards with byteIndex < permissionBytes.Length, so a role saved before this release reads the new permissions as false instead of throwing. Non-breaking, additive.",
